  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The text is a personal, autobiographical essay rather than an empirical research study.",
      "what": "This reflective essay traces the intellectual development of a geographer through four key texts read across different career stages and locations: Feminism & Geography in Dublin, The Wretched of the Earth in Kentucky, Even in Sweden in Nottingham, and Imperial Intimacies in Maynooth. The analysis explores how these works address feminism, colonialism, racism, and epistemology while offering frameworks for academic belonging and hope.",
      "why": "It documents the personal and emotional dimensions of geographic scholarship, demonstrating how foundational texts shape a researcher's identity and political commitment over time."
